# Session-local working state (large vector index, etc.) — never commit.
#
# T-2822: this is the CONTENTS form (`/*`), not the directory form. The directory
# form excluded `.context/working/` itself, and git cannot re-include a path whose
# parent directory is excluded — so a `!` negation under it is a SILENT no-op, not
# an error. Excluding the contents leaves the directory un-excluded, which is what
# makes the negation below bind at all.
#
# Why a negation is needed: 115 files under here are tracked. Ignore rules do not
# apply to already-tracked files, so nothing looked broken while every file added
# afterwards was silently untrackable. The casualties were the static-check
# allowlists (T-2527 alloc-sink, T-2531 drain-sink, T-2666 silent-exit, T-2672
# busy-spin, T-2821 cron-drift) — records of governance decisions that existed only
# on one host's disk, so both alloc-sink and drain-sink fired in every clean clone
# on sites a human had already reviewed and acknowledged.
#
# Re-included BY PATTERN, not by filename: the casualty is the whole class of checks
# following that convention, so the next one is trackable without another edit here.
# Everything else — vector index, session state, counters, logs — stays ignored.
.context/working/*
!.context/working/.*-allowlist

# Background-session git worktrees (T-2219: prevent accidental gitlink commits)
.claude/worktrees/

# ── T-2839 housekeeping ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTE: .gitignore has NO trailing-comment syntax. `*.deb  # why` is a literal
# pattern containing spaces and a hash, and matches nothing. The first version of
# this block was written that way and silently ignored nothing at all — caught by
# `git check-ignore -v`, which is why the rules below are asserted rather than
# assumed. Comments go on their own lines.

# Editor/script backups. 15 were loose in the tree: 13 byte-identical to their live
# file, one recoverable from a7625c1ff, one under .context/working/. Untracked
# residue is harmless right up until someone runs `git add -A`.
*.bak

# Downloaded packages. voxtype_0.7.5-1_amd64.deb (327MB) sits in the repo root
# today; a single `git add -A` writes it into history permanently.
*.deb

# Python bytecode ANYWHERE, not just under .agentic-framework/. A stale .pyc can
# shadow its source: python compares source mtime in whole SECONDS and size, so a
# same-size edit landing inside one second is invisible and the old bytecode is
# served. Measured in this repo — identical source, two different verdicts, decided
# only by whether __pycache__ existed.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
